cal Centre, there are no equivalent links with Bassetlaw Hospital.","summary":"Establish specialist eating disorder service for children and adolescents","timescale":"8 September 2015"}]},{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2015/07/2015-0276-Response-by-Doncaster-and-Bassettlaw-Hospitals-NHS-Trust.pdf","filename":"2015-0276-Response-by-Doncaster-and-Bassettlaw-Hospitals-NHS-Trust.pdf","promises":[{"id":1591,"quote":"We have an identified Consultant and will actively engage with the services provided by Nottinghamshire Healthcare Trust as the need arises and will monitor these arrangements through the paediatric clinical governance team.","summary":"Identified consultant to engage with Nottinghamshire Healthcare Trust and monitor arrangements via paediatric clinical governance team.","timescale":null}]}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/samantha-macdonald/","title":"Samantha MacDonald","date":"2016-02-05","coroner":"Jennifer Leeming","area":"Manchester (West)","ref":"2016-0036","categories":["Other related deaths","Suicide (from 2015)"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/03/2016-0036-Response-by-Department-fro-Business-Innovation-and-Skills.pdf","filename":"2016-0036-Response-by-Department-fro-Business-Innovation-and-Skills.pdf","promises":[],"unmatched":true},{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/02/2016-0036-Response-by-Campus-Living-Villages.pdf","filename":"2016-0036-Response-by-Campus-Living-Villages.pdf","promises":[],"unmatched":true}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/christopher-sears/","title":"Christopher Sears","date":"2016-05-25","coroner":"Karen Henderson","area":"Surrey","ref":"2016-0212","categories":["Child Death (from 2015)"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/05/2016-0212-Response-by-Department-for-Education.pdf","filename":"2016-0212-Response-by-Department-for-Education.pdf","promises":[{"id":556,"quote":"We intend to consult on a revised version of the guidance on school transport in the autumn. Subject to any responses received in response to this consultation, we will consider whether we should further clarify both the description of the training that drivers should undertake and our expectation that training for bus drivers and escorts should include basic life support training alongside the implementation of healthcare protocols, including emergency protocols.","summary":"Consult on revised school transport guidance in autumn","timescale":"autumn"}]}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/karnel-haughton/","title":"Karnel Haughton","date":"2016-09-23","coroner":"Emma Brown","area":"Birmingham and Solihull","ref":"2016-0339","categories":["Other related deaths"],"responses":[]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/jane-reason/","title":"Jane Reason","date":"2016-10-25","coroner":"Louise Hunt","area":"Birmingham and Solihull","ref":"2016-0376","categories":["Other related deaths"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/2016-0376-Response-by-British-Heart-Foundation.pdf","filename":"2016-0376-Response-by-British-Heart-Foundation.pdf","promises":[{"id":169,"quote":"The BHF has been a key partner in running national awareness campaigns about the importance of bystander CPR skills on \"European Restart a Heart Day\" for 3 years and have recently worked with a number of partners including the UK Resuscitation Council, British Red Cross, St John Ambulance and the 14 UK ambulance services to provide resources and support training of 150,000 young people in one day at a number of events across the UK on 18th October 2016","summary":"BHF trained 150,000 young people in CPR on 18 Oct 2016","timescale":"18th October 2016"}]},{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/2016-0376-Response-by-Department-for-Education.pdf","filename":"2016-0376-Response-by-Department-for-Education.pdf","promises":[]}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/chadrack-mulo/","title":"Chadrack Mulo","date":"2017-04-12","coroner":"ME Hassell","area":"London Inner (North)","ref":"2017-0120","categories":["Child Death (from 2015)","Other related deaths"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/2017-0120-Response-by-Department-for-Education.pdf","filename":"2017-0120-Response-by-Department-for-Education.pdf","promises":[{"id":1354,"quote":"have asked Departmental officials to examine how we can best update the statutory 'Keeping Children Safe in Education' guidance and the 'School Attendance' guidance so that they reflect best practice and recommend that schools hold more than one contact number. You","summary":"Update guidance to require multiple contact numbers for pupils","timescale":null}]}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/abdul-jamal-ottun/","title":"Abdul-Jamal Ottun","date":"2018-01-18","coroner":"Andrew Harris","area":"London Inner (South)","ref":"2018-0020","categories":["Other related deaths"],"responses":[{"pdf_url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/2018-0020-Response-by-Department-for-Education.pdf","filename":"2018-0020-Response-by-Department-for-Education.pdf","promises":[{"id":1145,"quote":"we tasked an independent group of experts from across the swimming sector to submit an independent report seiting out recommendations for improving curriculum swimming as part of the Sporting Future strategy. The group published their report in July 2017 and we subsequently established an implementation group, and are currently reviewing the recommendations in the report. In","summary":"Review recommendations from independent swimming report","timescale":"July 2017"}]}]},{"url":"https://www.judiciary.uk/prevention-of-future-death-reports/ben-walmsley/","title":"Ben Walmsley","d